  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National social protection floor established and effectively functional in Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Liberia, the incidence of poverty is high, and poverty is predominantly a rural phenomenon. The government has tried to address the issue of poverty and inequality through different strategies. Social protection can help to reduce inequalities in Liberian society by re-distributing wealth among different income groups, however social protection programmes in Liberia consists of a fragmented group of uncoordinated, often small-scale interventions which are mostly dependent the sector on donor financing. Hence social protection schemes are accessed more by people in the formal sector and living in the urban areas. The ILO working with other UUN Agencies are implanting a programme that support government&#x2019;s progress towards achieving the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), including SDG 1: Zero Poverty, SDG 2: Zero Hunger; SDG 5: Gender Equality; SDG 8: Decent Jobs and Economic Growth; SDG 13: Climate Action; and SDG 17: Partnership for the Goals.
The Strategy of the intervention includes policy advice, training, skills development and digital services. The intervention will improve access to social protection as well as extending social protection coverage</narrative>
  </description>
